    'Supermarket systems require industrial-grade PoE infrastructure, enterprise servers, and precise optical calibration. We design turnkey systems engineered for continuous 24/7 reliability.',
    'We install for regional chains and independent grocers across the whole Fort Worth trade area, from large-format stores along I-20, I-35W, and Loop 820 to neighborhood markets in Haltom City, White Settlement, Saginaw, and east Fort Worth, and outward into Keller, Southlake, Colleyville, Burleson, Mansfield, Arlington, and Grand Prairie. Interstate-adjacent stores get heavier entrance facial capture and parking-lot plate coverage because organized crews move between Tarrant County corridors quickly. Neighborhood stores get more emphasis on the dock, the compactor, and the cart corrals. All work meets Tarrant County and City of Fort Worth commercial low-voltage requirements, and we coordinate landlord and property manager approvals before any roof or exterior wall penetration. Exterior hardware is specified for North Texas hail, ultraviolet load, and triple-digit summers, with enterprise recorders kept in conditioned space on battery backup. Fort Worth based crews mean same-day service calls and same-day evidence export when police request footage.',
