    'Jewelry store security systems must meet stringent insurance underwriting guidelines. Our licensed Fort Worth technicians install hardwired PoE systems inside metal conduit with battery backup UPS units and encrypted storage.',
    'We work with fine jewelers, diamond merchants, bridal specialists, and custom watchmakers in Downtown Fort Worth and the Sundance Square area, along Camp Bowie and Hulen Street, at Clearfork and Ridgmar, near TCU, and out through Southlake, Colleyville, Keller, and Grapevine. Street-level downtown storefronts get vestibule and sidewalk coverage priority, while managed-center locations get designs built around landlord rules for storefront and roof penetrations, which we clear with property management before any work begins. All installations meet Tarrant County and City of Fort Worth commercial low-voltage requirements. Exterior hardware is specified for North Texas hail, UV load, and triple-digit summer heat, with recorders kept in conditioned, locked space on battery backup. Because our technicians are based in Fort Worth, we can be on site for a service call and export evidence-grade footage for a police report or an underwriter the same day it is needed.',
